    <statement><tabular valign="top">
<row>
<cell>The surface <m>z = f(x,y)</m> is shown in the diagram.  
The green point is <m>A = (-2,2,0)</m> and the red point
is <m>B = (2,2,0)</m>.
(a) Are the following quantities positive, negative, or zero?<ol>
<li>
<m>f_y(B)</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>f_x(B)</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>f_y(A)</m>
</li>
<li>
<m>f_x(A)</m>
</li>
</ol>
(b) Suppose a point <m>P</m> in the xy-plane moves in a straight line 
from the green point <m>A</m> to the red point 
<m>B</m>.  <ol>
<li>
Does the sign of <m>f_y(P)</m> change from positive to negative, negative to positive, or is there no change in sign?
</li>
<li>
Does the sign of <m>f_x(P)</m> change from positive to negative, negative to positive, or is there no change in sign?
</li>
</ol></cell>
